  "query_preview": "../Sunday through Wednesday/...No change in message to\nthe Sunday forecast, still looking at a somewhat uncertain\ntemperature forecast, but leaning towards more dry weather for the\novernight period, which would hamper any fog development, which\nwould lead towards the higher max temperature. \n\nGoing into the work week next week, the marine threat returns.\nModels have generally locked onto the strong system in the\nnorthern Pacific, southern gulf solution. The one portion of\nuncertainty is the magnitude of the wind speeds for the southern\nportion of our AOR. Some solutions had storm force sustained winds\nfor the southern zones, decided to opt out of that solution and\nsettled for now on strong gales for the Monday Tuesday timeframe.\nFor the inner waters, this means stronger northerlies,\nparticularly for Lynn Canal, Taiya Inlet, and even out of Stikine\nRiver basin. At this time, the stronger winds look to be around\n20-30 knots, with highest wind speeds in Lynn Canal.",
